    "turn_text": "knocked an incumbent out for Chairman of the County Board. That's our equivalent of mayor. It's a county of a million people, so it's a big deal. A beat or two to one. I swept in a Republican board for the only time in history. And I had, you know, I just, getting elected and governing are really two different skill sets. I faced a huge debt crisis in the county and stuff, and we resolved it. We got selected best financially managed county in the country, and I fit, well, what else can I do? And we had a democratic incumbent sitting in the middle of my district, and I took her on and beat her. I beat her in 1994, which was a Republican here nationally, but it was not in the urban centers in Virginia. So, and we had two congressional candidates that had run in 92 and ran again in 94. They both did worse in 94. One, Kyle McSlero in the 8th District and one in the 2nd District, Jim Chapman, and my district was worse too, but, but, and I had all over North at the top of the ticket, and he got 29% in my district. But we, I had a good local base, I had the endorsement of the Washington Post, I had the business community behind me, and I wanted 54-45.",
