    "turn_text": "know getting elected, if you work hard and you know your constituents, so my constituents disagreed with me on impeachment, they disagreed with me on a minimum wage. You disagreed with me on the life issue, but I did a lot of other things. I talked about the things we had in common. I was able to deliver for them and it didn't, you know, at the end of the day, and they never really laid a glove on me. My last re-elect, I was down to 56%, but my Senate candidate, Georgia Allen, who's running for reelection at 42%. So I faced a huge draft, you know, a wave coming at me, and I still managed to to finesse it. But my wife had lost her seat in the state Senate after 10 years, and I just said to me, I was turned out as a committee chairman and said let's have a life. Let's have a life. And I'd had a job offer for a million bucks when I was in Congress that I toyed with, but the leadership said, we need you to keep your seat. And I said, you know, I think I can do well out here. And I suffered from a disease called maltuition. your parents probably suffer from the same disease. And so, I thought, you know, this is the time to replenish the coffers and move ahead. And so, I went out, I got a job with, do what gave me a generous offer. I served on a couple of boards and I spent the next 10 years kind of building some wealth. So, for my kids, so I could have a comfortable life and my wife won't let me quit working, so I'm still working.",
