  {
    "episode_id": 91625,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91625.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "I have just so many members. One of my favorites, I'm working on a bowling alley, because at nine o'clock there's nothing else to do. You can work bingo games. You can get a lot of hands at bingo games, but once they start calling, bingo games are 95% old women. After nine o'clock you could go to bowling alleys and I would just go in I start going down the lanes and shaking hands with everybody and one guy said he's a big guy. He says I ain't voting for you. And I said well why not because I'm a convicted felon. So I didn't get him. And look, what you've got to do is you can't react if somebody says something bad. That's the worst thing. You can, particularly now in the YouTube times, you can't. So you just have to be programmed, but you're going to get a certain percentage to give you the finger or tell you they hate your guts or they don't like it. And you just smile at them and I was programmed to say, well, you know, if I can never do anything to help you, I hope you'll call me. And you just go on to the next one, you go home and kick the dog. But that's how you have to handle that. And so many people make the mistake of going back or trying to say something smart. And you want to inside, but I learned early on that there's no percentage in that. And you're just not everybody's good to vote for you.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Not everyone will support or vote for me, and that is expected.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Reacting negatively to criticism is the worst possible response in current public discourse.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Some people will respond with aggression or disdain regardless of effort.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "I am currently working on a project involving a bowling alley.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "It is necessary to remain emotionally neutral when encountering hostility during outreach efforts.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Bingo games typically attract mostly older women after nine o'clock.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "One person explicitly refused to vote for me because I am a convicted felon.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker has been trained or conditioned to maintain composure under hostile interactions.",
