    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "it's two things. I think it's the change in the issue matrix that the Republican Party has emphasized. When you move to social issues in these affluent areas, you get a little bit of a backlash. If you go with economic issues. that's different. And so I emphasized the economic issues as I voted against minimum wage laws. I have a free trader, very anti-regulation. My economic record was as conservative as anybody's in Virginia. In the Virginia delegation, we had a number of conservatives. My social record was more mixed. I was pro-life, but I also voted for endo, which was the Indiscrimination Plavement Act. You didn't discriminate against gays. When I was on the county board, the board took off, took away the gay newspapers and the libraries, I put them back in. I said, the libraries are for everybody. We don't make these kind of judgments. I represent everybody. And when somebody said, oh, you took a contribution from so long, I said, I speak to everybody. I represent everybody. And that was kind of my mantra. So I had a very inclusive group. I put the first Asian on a school board in Virginia when we put the first Hispanic on a school board in Virginia. I reached out to the communities that had been ignored for a long time and kind of brought them into the fold. Their values were as conservative as anybody. You know the mosque, you won't find a more conservative group than your muscles on issues like marriage and just in general, very family oriented. They're turning off and pushing the mute button on Republicans because of immigration or maybe the war in the Middle East or something else. You got to talk about what binds you together. And I stood up for them. They had some zoning difficulties out there. Nobody wanted a mosque in their neighborhood. And I said, well, we have Christian churches across the street. Of course, they're entitled to the place. So I built some bridges doing those kind of things. And people may not have agreed with me on everything, but they always thought they could get a fair shake.",
