    "turn_text": "all the time. I mean, even on the College Access Act, which I talked about, I also found some school vouchers for the city, which are still there. That was passed the House by one vote. Never passed the Senate, but we folded it into an appropriation bill and it went through in that way. But when people come up to you and said, you know, I went to College Access Act, allowed me to go to college, that made a difference. When I built the first homeless shelter in Fairfax County, a lady came up to me. She said, you know, my husband had beaten me up. I didn't have anywhere to go. I had two kids that went to this shelter and it gave me a couple months and I could get back in my feet. I really appreciate you because nobody wants a homeless shelter in their district. I can tell you that. And I took the heat from the local neighbors because we had a man freeze to death on Christmas night at Bailey's Crossroads. I said, we can't allow this to happen in our county. We're better than that. And we started it that way.",
